From bbac7d7ae1f221d8e00cb476acd7fc5b41b1a383 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jarojarojaro-jaro <miki.jaroszek@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 01:09:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/7] speculative: --spec-draft-vocab also restricts the
 DFlash/DFlash2 drafter's LM head (the target's output rows)

The DFlash drafter borrows the target's output matrix (Qwen3.8: Q6_K 248320 x 5120, ~1.04 GB read per draft
step, all block positions). With --spec-draft-vocab the restricted copy of the target's output rows
(set_draft_head_vocab, the MTP draft head slot) scores only the listed tokens: DFlash2 runs its top-k selector on
the restricted logits and maps the candidates back to token ids (no -inf fill); DFlash1 (sampled logits) scatters
into -inf logits as the MTP head does. Verification unchanged, so lossless; drafts are restricted to the list.
Default unchanged (no --spec-draft-vocab for DFlash in run-llm.sh).

UNMEASURED (no GPU access at commit time).
